// expect: 9
// SYNTAX §«Pattern syntax for records» through a PARAMETER — the twin of
// record-pattern-local. `let {zeta} = u` binds by the field's NAME, and a
// parameter's record is open: the caller decides the fields beside `zeta`,
// so the slot is known only under the twin the call keys. The pattern read
// the slot from its own enumeration index instead, and answered 7 — alpha's
// value — with no diagnostic (`Hβ.lower.record-pattern-param-receiver`,
// measured 2026-08-17).
fn pick(u) = {
  let {zeta} = u
  zeta
}

fn main() = pick({alpha: 7, zeta: 9})
